course: dictionary
lesson: 1591
title: Cheat: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Cheat» can be a verb, meaning what someone does, or a noun, meaning a person. Read the words around it to find out which. Then check by swapping in your meaning and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Handing in work you did not do, from a person, a website or an AI chatbot, is cheating.» Here cheating is an action. The clue is «handing in work you did not do»: it means passing off someone else's work as your own.
explain: «If you see a friend cheat, loyalty and fairness clash.» Here cheat is a verb meaning to break the rules to get an advantage. The clue is that cheating is set against fairness, so it must be unfair.
explain: Cheat can also mean to trick someone, often to get their money. Saying someone cheated without proof is unfair, so the sentence around the word shows how serious it is. Always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cheat» can be a verb (to cheat) or a noun (a cheat, meaning a person who cheats).
fact: To cheat means to break the rules to win or get an advantage, or to trick someone.
fact: A «cheat sheet» is a list of helpful notes, and you may use one only when the teacher says so.
fact: In stories, cheats are usually caught in the end.
exercise: «Owning up and asking for help with the part you didn't understand is the real fix for cheating in learning.» According to this sentence, what is cheating in learning? | Asking the teacher a question | Reading slowly | *Copying someone's work or looking at answers | Writing a neat summary
exercise: «At the ancient Olympic Games, cheats paid fines that built bronze statues of Zeus.» In this sentence, what is a cheat? | The name of a sports game | A bronze statue of Zeus | *A person who broke the rules to win
exercise: «If you see a friend cheat, loyalty and fairness clash; a good first step is often to talk to your friend.» What is a good first step if you see a friend cheat? | Copy them | *Talk to your friend | Tell nobody and forget it ever happened | Shout at them in front of everyone
test: What is a cheat sheet? | *A list of helpful notes, allowed only when the teacher says | A sheet of paper with nothing on it | A plate for cheese | A test that is very hard
test: «Saying someone cheated without proof is unfair; if nobody saw it, drop it.» What should you do if nobody saw the cheating? | Shout the accusation loudly | *Drop it | Make them pay a fine | Tell the whole class
exam: Which word means to break the rules to win? | *Cheat | Loyal | Clash | Fair
